course: dictionary
lesson: 1015
title: Sound words and many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words sound like the thing they describe. «Bonk» is one of them: say it out loud and it sounds like a light knock. When a word has more than one meaning, read the words around it. «An apple bonks Newton on the head» tells you someone was hit gently on the head, so bonk fits.
explain: The clues change the meaning. «Cyclists and runners say they bonked» in a long race. The race and the word energy tell you bonk here means running out of energy, not being hit. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence? Then try it in the sentence to check.
explain: In «Tom gets bonked on the head, sees stars and birds spinning round, and is fine a second later», the cartoon clues show a silly, light knock. A real hard knock can shake the brain, which is called concussion, and needs rest and a doctor. Adults sometimes use bonk as a rude joke word, so if you hear it that way, ask a grown-up.
fact: «Bonk» (informal) means to hit someone or something lightly, often on the head.
fact: A «bonk» can be the light hit itself, or the sound it makes.
fact: In sport, to «bonk» or «hit the wall» means to suddenly run out of energy in a long race.
fact: A real hard knock to the head can shake the brain; this is called concussion and needs rest and a doctor.
fact: Some slang words are rude; if you are not sure about a word, ask a grown-up.
exercise: «An apple bonks Newton on the head.» What does bonks mean here? | To shout loudly | To fall asleep | *To hit lightly on the head | To run very fast
exercise: Cyclists say they «bonked» in a long race. What does bonked mean in sport? | *Suddenly ran out of energy | Won the race easily | Laughed loudly at a joke | Hit someone on the head
exercise: Tom gets bonked on the head and sees stars in a cartoon. Is this a real hard knock or a funny cartoon knock? | A real hard knock that needs a doctor | *A funny, light cartoon knock | A race where someone ran out of energy
test: «Tom gets bonked on the head, sees stars, and is fine a second later.» What is the best meaning of bonked here? | *A light, funny knock | A loud shout | A long, slow race | A kind pat on the back
test: A real hard knock can shake the brain. What is this called? | Energy | Cartoon | Bonk | *Concussion
exam: Ella says «bonk» is always rude. What is the best answer? | Yes, it is always rude, so never use it | *No, it has several meanings, and the rude one is only one of them | Yes, but only in cartoons | No, it only ever means a race
